  <section id="mechanism" class="briefing-slide tone-gold" aria-labelledby="mechanism-title">
    <div class="slide-inner taskvector-slide">
      <h2 id="mechanism-title">{t('训练确实在发生以后，新的问题是：参数到底学到了什么？', 'Once training was clearly happening, the next question was: what did the parameters actually learn?')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('TaskVector 把两个参数状态之间的变化写成一个向量。这样我们可以从“更新了多少次”继续追问“更新朝哪个方向走、相邻更新是否一致、这个方向是否真的会改变行为”。', 'TaskVector writes the change between two parameter states as a vector. That lets us move from counting updates to asking which direction they move, whether successive updates align, and whether that direction actually changes behavior.')}</p>
      <div class="taskvector-equation" aria-label={t('TaskVector 定义', 'TaskVector definition')}>
        <span>TaskVector</span>
        <strong>v = θ<sub>after</sub> − θ<sub>before</sub></strong>
        <p>{t('θ 表示模型参数；v 就是一次学习前后，参数真正移动的方向。', 'θ denotes model parameters; v is the direction the parameters actually moved during learning.')}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><strong>{t('看长度', 'measure magnitude')}</strong><p>{t('‖v‖ 告诉我们参数移动了多少。', '‖v‖ tells us how much the parameters moved.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><strong>{t('看方向', 'compare direction')}</strong><p>{t('比较相邻 TaskVector 的夹角 / cosine，看连续更新是否朝相近方向。', 'Compare angles / cosine between successive TaskVectors to see whether updates point similarly.')}</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><strong>{t('再做因果干预', 'then test causally')}</strong><p>{t('把同一个方向正向或反向施加，观察 WebShop 行为是否随方向改变。', 'Apply the same direction forward or backward and observe whether WebShop behavior follows the direction.')}</p></article>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-stability">
        <strong>{t('1.7B 的 7 次正式更新不是一直同向；最近一次才明显对齐。', 'The seven formal 1.7B updates are not all aligned; the latest one is the clearly aligned step.')}</strong>
        <p>{t('从第二次更新开始，相邻方向相似度大约是 0.56 → 0.35 → 0.03 → -0.02 → 0.11 → 0.79。前半段像是在到处试路；最后一次和前一次很一致，说明后期可能开始沿着更稳定的参数方向移动。', 'From the second update onward, adjacent direction similarity is about 0.56 → 0.35 → 0.03 → -0.02 → 0.11 → 0.79. The early segment looks exploratory; the latest admitted update is strongly aligned with the previous one, suggesting a more stable parameter direction may be emerging.')}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="taskvector-causal">
        <div><strong>24 / 24</strong><span>{t('拿掉累计 SD-LoRA 参数变化以后，固定 24 个输入的第一选择全部翻转', 'After removing the accumulated SD-LoRA parameter change, the top choice flipped on all 24 fixed inputs')}</span></div>
        <div><strong>0.15 → 1.02</strong><span>{t('对原本目标行为的拟合 loss 明显变差', 'fit loss on the original target behavior became much worse')}</span></div>
        <p>{t('这个 post-hoc 参数干预说明：这些累计参数变化已经真正进入模型决策过程。它证明“参数方向会改变行为”，不等于证明这些方向全部都在提高最终 WebShop 分数。', 'This post-hoc parameter intervention shows that the accumulated parameter change is behaviorally active in the model. It establishes that the parameter direction changes decisions; it does not establish that every such direction improves the final WebShop score.')}</p>
        <a href={measurementPackHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><ExternalBrandMark href={measurementPackHref} /> PR #317 · {t('参数机制分析', 'parameter-mechanism analysis')}</a>
      </div>
      <p class="taskvector-paper"><strong>{t('参考思想', 'Reference idea')}</strong><a href={taskArithmeticHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ilharco et al. · Editing Models with Task Arithmetic ↗</a><span>{t('论文把微调前后的参数差看成权重空间方向；我们进一步追踪 OpenEVO 连续自我训练产生的一系列方向。', 'The paper treats the before/after fine-tuning difference as a direction in weight space; we extend that idea to a sequence of OpenEVO self-training updates.')}</span></p>
      <p class="slide-bridge">{t('完整 Gram matrix、Frobenius 范数、R14 / R27 / R49 构造和随机同范数对照都留在技术页。', 'The full Gram matrix, Frobenius norm, R14 / R27 / R49 construction, and norm-matched random controls remain in the technical notes.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('TaskVector 完整推导与实验门槛', 'Full TaskVector derivation and experimental thresholds')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">14 / 19</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="gdr" class="briefing-slide tone-rose" aria-labelledby="gdr-title">
    <div class="slide-inner">
      <h2 id="gdr-title">{t('OpenEVO 准备用 SD-LoRA 更新参数时，GDR 作为 gate 决定是否真的更新', 'When OpenEVO prepares an SD-LoRA parameter update, GDR acts as the gate that decides whether it is applied')}</h2>
      <p class="slide-thesis">{t('GDR = Gated Delta Rule。这里要分清两层：论文里的 Gated Delta Rule 是一种“擦掉旧关联、写入新关联”的快速记忆更新；我们真正跑的 GDR-v1 没有把 SD-LoRA 直接套进论文的 S / k / v 公式，而是把已经训练好的完整候选状态送去做一次短期小考，再决定要不要采用。', 'GDR = Gated Delta Rule. Two layers matter here: the paper’s gated delta rule is a fast-memory update that erases an old association and writes a new one; our executed GDR-v1 did not directly plug SD-LoRA into the paper’s S / k / v equation. It trained a complete candidate state, ran a short probe, and then decided whether to adopt it.')}</p>
      <div class="gdr-paper-map" aria-label={t('Gated Delta Rule 论文里的变量', 'Variables in the Gated Delta Rule paper')}>
        <div><span>S</span><strong>{t('快速记忆状态', 'fast-memory state')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>k</span><strong>{t('要改写的关联位置 / key', 'association address / key')}</strong></div>
        <div><span>v</span><strong>{t('准备写入的新 value', 'new value to write')}</strong></div>
        <p>{t('论文更新会沿 k 对应方向修正旧关联，再写入 v；gating 还控制整体记忆衰减。这个 S / k / v 是论文的 fast-weight memory 语义，不是 OpenEVO Stage 2 的可执行状态字段。', 'The paper corrects the old association along k and writes v, while gating controls state decay. These S / k / v symbols belong to the paper’s fast-weight memory semantics; they are not executable OpenEVO Stage-2 state fields.')}</p>
        <a href={gatedDeltaPaperHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Yang et al. · Gated Delta Networks ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="before-after gdr-flow">
        <div class="before"><span>{t('论文给我们的启发', 'paper inspiration')}</span><strong>{t('先修正旧记忆，再写入新信息', 'correct old memory, then write new information')}</strong><p>{t('所以你记得的“erase 旧的，再 add 新的”这个直觉是对的；它来自 Gated Delta Rule 本身的记忆更新思路。', 'So your memory of “erase the old, then add the new” is the right intuition for the original gated-delta memory update.')}</p></div>
        <div class="after"><span>{t('我们真正跑的 GDR-v1', 'our executed GDR-v1')}</span><strong>{t('旧状态与完整候选各做 16-task probe，再决定是否换状态', 'probe incumbent and full candidate on 16 tasks, then decide whether to switch')}</strong><p>{t('候选的 exact success、positive score、mean score 都不能退步，invalid 也不能变差，而且至少一个任务指标必须严格提高；否则下一轮继续用旧状态。', 'The candidate cannot regress on exact success, positive score, or mean score, invalids cannot worsen, and at least one task metric must strictly improve; otherwise the next round keeps the incumbent state.')}</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="gdr-why-gate"><strong>{t('为什么最后变成了 gate？', 'Why did it become a gate?')}</strong>{t('我们当时没有可靠办法直接判断“哪段参数是错的、该擦多少、哪段是新的正确方向”。于是先用可测的短期任务表现作为保守替代：候选先训练，再由 probe 决定生死。这个选择后来又带来新的科学问题——短期不变差的要求，会不会把长期有价值的学习路径提前截断？', 'We did not have reliable evidence for which parameter direction was wrong, how much to erase, or which new direction was correct. So we used a conservative measurable surrogate: train the candidate first, then let the probe decide whether it survives. That design created the next scientific question—does requiring immediate non-regression cut off learning paths that would become valuable later?')}</p>
      <p class="bottom-claim">{t('因此我们把两个计数分开看：OpenEVO 到底训练出了多少个 SD-LoRA 候选，以及 GDR 最终让多少个候选真正更新到后续模型。下一页就是 1.7B 正式线的实际结果。', 'We therefore track two counts separately: how many SD-LoRA candidates OpenEVO actually trained, and how many GDR allowed to update later model states. The next slide shows the formal 1.7B result.')}</p>
      <p class="source-note"><a href={technicalHref}>{t('GDR 的完整判定逻辑与实验定义', 'Full GDR decision logic and experiment definition')}</a></p>
      <p class="slide-number">15 / 19</p>
    </div>
  </section>
